# The build context is what `COPY . .` bakes into the image, and the timer rebuilds on every
# run (`--build`). Without this file the context was ~2.9 GB: the 2.2 GB fastembed model under
# .cache (which compose mounts over anyway), the host .venv, mypy's cache — and .env and
# secrets/, i.e. the Gmail OAuth token, inside an image layer. Any change to those directories
# invalidated the layer, so a local `mypy` run cost the next timer tick a 3 GB layer export;
# on 2026-10-19 that export swapped the machine and never finished. Runtime inputs come in
# through compose instead: env_file for .env, bind mounts for data/ and secrets/.
.git
.githooks
.idea
.claude
.venv
.cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
.env
secrets
data
tests
